Kubernetes[EKS] Pod Error List🟪

 📌Have you ever faced errors in Kubernetes? 


🎯 Image & Pull Errors
➡️ ImagePullBackOff → Kubernetes tried pulling the image but failed repeatedly.

➡️ ErrImagePull → Image pull failed (authentication error, image not found, registry unavailable).

➡️ InvalidImageName → The container image name or tag is invalid.

➡️ RegistryUnavailable → Image registry is temporarily down or unreachable.

➡️ ErrImageNeverPull → Pull policy set to Never but the image is not present on the node.

🎯 Container Crash & Restart Errors
➡️ CrashLoopBackOff → Container starts, crashes, and keeps restarting.

➡️ RunContainerError → Failed to run the container after creation.

➡️ ErrContainerStart → General container start failure.

➡️ ContainerCannotRun → Command or entrypoint in the container is invalid.

➡️ OOMKilled → Container killed due to exceeding memory limit.

Error → Container process exited with a non-zero exit code.

Completed → Container finished execution successfully (common in Jobs).

🎯 Scheduling & Placement Errors
➡️ Pending → Pod scheduled but not running due to resource constraints.

➡️ Unschedulable → No suitable node found (resource requests too high, taints not tolerated).

Evicted → Pod removed from node due to resource pressure (disk, memory, node drain).

🎯 Readiness & Liveness Probe Failures
➡️Unhealthy → Failing readiness or liveness probes.

➡️Readiness probe failed → Pod marked as not ready.

➡️ Liveness probe failed → Container restarted due to failing health check.

🎯 Volume & Mount Errors
➡️ CreateContainerConfigError → Issue creating container config (often volume-related).

➡️ MountVolume.SetUp failed → Failed to attach/mount a volume.

➡️ VolumeMountConflict → Multiple containers mounting the same volume path incorrectly.

PVC not found → Pod references a PersistentVolumeClaim that doesn’t exist.

FailedAttachVolume / FailedMount → EBS/EFS volume could not be attached/mounted.

🎯 Init Container Failures
➡️Init:CrashLoopBackOff → Init container repeatedly crashes.

➡️ Init:Error → Init container exits with error.

➡️ Init:ImagePullBackOff → Init container image cannot be pulled.

🎯 Security & Policy Errors
➡️ CreateContainerError → Pod sandbox creation failed (often security policy related).

Forbidden → Pod creation blocked by RBAC, PodSecurityPolicy, or OPA/Gatekeeper.
